	(text "Test Points -- bring-up probing"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.046 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
		)
		(uuid "88888888-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "Placement only: no wires or global labels yet.\n\nThis board's whole difficulty is sub-nanosecond timing and per-anchor delay\ncalibration, and bring-up will involve real measurement against real\nhardware. Without probe points that measurement is guesswork. These cost\nnothing now and cannot be added after layout.\n\nChosen for the specific risks this design actually has:\n\n  CLOCK -- the defining signal. If the shared reference is absent, wrong\n  frequency, or missing at one anchor, TDoA silently produces nonsense\n  rather than failing loudly. TP5 checks the TCXO itself; TP6-TP9 confirm\n  the buffer actually reaches each of the four DW3210 XTI pins.\n\n  SPI -- the driver work (restoring multi-instance support) is on the\n  critical path and will need a logic analyser. TP10-TP12 give it somewhere\n  to clip on. TP13 (A0 IRQ) and TP14 (shared anchor reset) make the\n  exchange timing visible.\n\n  POWER -- TP1/TP2 confirm the rails before anything else is debugged.\n\n  GROUND -- TWO of them, deliberately. TP3 sits next to the clock points so\n  a scope probe can use a short ground spring rather than a long flying\n  lead; at 38.4MHz a clip lead's inductance distorts what you are trying to\n  measure. TP4 is a general-purpose ground elsewhere on the board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.364 51.308 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "88888888-0000-4000-8000-000000000002")
	)
	(text "LAYOUT NOTE, important: a test point on the clock network is a STUB, and\nstubs degrade exactly the signal integrity this design depends on. Keep\nTP5-TP9 as small pads with the shortest possible stub -- ideally a bare\nprobe pad rather than a through-hole post -- and place them ON the existing\nrouting rather than spurring off it where possible. If a clean layout\ncannot accommodate all four anchor clock points, drop TP8/TP9 and keep\nTP6/TP7: two is enough to compare skew between channels."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 112.268 87.63 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "88888888-0000-4000-8000-000000000003")
	)
